      "topLeftX": 183,
      "topLeftY": 457,
      "bottomRightX": 696,
      "bottomRightY": 528,
      "content": "This example shows one way a PIPE PHY can be controlled to perform Active State Power Management on a link for the sequence of the link being in L0 state, transitioning to L1 state, and then transitioning back to L0 state. This example assumes that the PHY is on an endpoint (that is, it is facing upstream) and that the endpoint has met all the requirements (as specified in the base specification) for entering L1.",
